# Clariti Electron App Design Language

Apply this rule only to the Electron app in `frontend/`. Do not apply it to `landingsite/` or other website/marketing UI.

## Visual Direction

- Use an editorial, quiet interface: generous whitespace, compact controls, thin borders, and subtle elevation.
- Use `font-serif` only for high-emphasis page headings and motivational/empty-state copy. Keep labels, controls, and body copy sans-serif.
- The canonical app heading style is `font-serif text-3xl font-light tracking-tight text-foreground` (used by “Projects”); apply it to titles that should match that hierarchy, including the Create Project dialog title.
- Prefer rounded `lg`/`xl` cards and controls. Avoid heavy gradients or decorative backgrounds unless the user supplies an asset or requests one.

## Surfaces and Colors

- App content canvas: `#fafafd`.
- Sidebar and cards: pure white (`#ffffff`).
- Separators and card borders: `#ececf1`.
- Soft form/control fill: `#f5f5f8`.
- Primary dark text and CTA: `#111114` / `#15151b`; hover CTA: `#29292f`.
- Use existing pastel icon/status colors sparingly for semantic distinction.

## Layout and Assets

- Maintain a clearly separated white sidebar with a thin right border against the off-white content canvas.
- Give cards a thin border and soft shadow, such as `shadow-[0_2px_8px_rgba(15,15,25,0.05)]`.
- Use `/logo.png` for Clariti product branding; do not substitute a generic flask icon for a brand mark.
- Keep functional icons for actions such as Create Test, Execute, and project status.

## Modals

- Use a structured three-region layout for form modals: a bordered header (`px-6 py-5`), a padded body (`px-6 py-5`), and a bordered action footer (`px-6 py-4`).
- Set structured `DialogContent` to `gap-0 p-0`, then apply spacing within each region; do not rely on the dialog's default padding and gap.
- Modal titles use `font-serif text-2xl font-light`; descriptions remain compact sans-serif text.
- Keep primary modal actions dark (`bg-[#111114] hover:bg-[#29292f]`) and secondary actions outlined.
- For long read-only content, cap the dialog at `max-h-[80vh]` and make only its body scrollable. Keep the title/header fixed.
- On cards, cap long previews at `max-h-56 overflow-hidden`, add a subtle bottom fade, and provide a “View full …” action that opens the read-only dialog.

## Example

```tsx
<DialogContent className="max-w-lg gap-0 p-0">
  <DialogHeader className="border-b border-[#ececf1] px-6 py-5" />
  <div className="px-6 py-5">{/* form fields */}</div>
  <DialogFooter className="border-t border-[#ececf1] px-6 py-4" />
</DialogContent>
```
